CURRENT RELEASE: gPLUTO 0.89 (Dec 2025)

************************************************************************
This is the 2nd beta release of the gPLUTO code, a full C++ rewrite 
of the PLUTO code, and capable of running on both multiple CPUs and GPUs. 

Algorithms not supported or in development stage:

-  Adaptive Mesh refinement (development)
-  Cooling                  (development)
-  CHARACTERISTIC_TRACING   (not supported)
-  HANCOCK                  (not supported)
-  SHEARINGBOX              (not supported)
-  FINITE DIFFERENCE        (not supported)

Main notation differences:

- Staggered arrays start from zero ("i" means "i-1/2" instead of "i+1/2");
- Reduced usage of global variables, replaced with the RunConfig 
  structure;
- Grid definition in [pluto.ini] has changed;
- Global coordinate indices IBEG, IEND, JBEG, JEND have been removed and replaced by 
  extensive usage of RBox structures;
- Limiter is unique for all variables;
- CYLINDRICAL Geometry can be used for both (r,phi) or (r,z).
  For the latter simply set DIMENSIONS == 3 and set INCLUDE_JDIR to NO.
************************************************************************

